Subject: [PATCH 09/29] Escape the apostrophe in the new English string

aapt2 rejects a bare one inside a resource as an invalid escape sequence.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml b/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml
index cd60287..672c52b 100644
--- a/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml
+++ b/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml
@@ -2178,5 +2178,5 @@
     <string name="gpu_safety_boot_blind">The boot reason could not be read (%1$s), so the guard cannot see a crash from the phone itself. It detects one from its own record instead: a session left running when the uptime went backwards.</string>
     <string name="gpu_safety_probe_required">Treat a probe that could not run as a failure</string>
     <string name="gpu_safety_probe_required_hint">If the GPU cannot be tested, do not start Steam. Off, a skipped probe launches anyway - which is how a session reaches the kernel with nothing having been shown to work.</string>
-    <string name="gpu_guard_probe_skipped_blocked">The GPU test could not be run, so Steam was not started. Turn it off in Setup, Safety, or create the file droiddeck-no-gpu-probe in the app's folder.</string>
+    <string name="gpu_guard_probe_skipped_blocked">The GPU test could not be run, so Steam was not started. Turn it off in Setup, Safety, or create the file droiddeck-no-gpu-probe in the app\'s folder.</string>
 </resources>
